implementationPlan.description:
Fix caller attribution with test-first regression coverage (DoD 1–2). Load test-driven-development; reuse ToolTestHarness and existing beforeEach/afterEach cleanup. Add a schema assertion that workerId is type string, is not required, and additionalProperties remains false. Add compact parameterized cases for governor-1, qa-1 and architect-1 differing from assigned worker-1; explicit caller on an unassigned task; omitted caller with assigned worker-1; omitted caller with null assignee yielding 'unknown'; and empty-string caller retaining the same legacy fallback. For each case seed with h.createTask({ assignedWorkerId: assignee }); await h.state.load(); invoke ADD_RAIL/GLOBAL with the optional caller field only when supplied, assert the created proposal's workerId using the returned proposalId, then reload and assert the exact same value. Also assert the task assignee is unchanged. Example core assertion:
```ts
const result = await proposeRailTool(h.state).handler({ taskId: 'task-1', proposalType: 'ADD_RAIL', targetScope: 'GLOBAL', proposedValue: 'test rail', reason: 'test attribution', workerId: 'governor-1' }, h.state) as { proposalId: string };
expect(h.state.proposals.get(result.proposalId)?.workerId).toBe('governor-1');
await h.state.load();
expect(h.state.proposals.get(result.proposalId)?.workerId).toBe('governor-1');
expect(h.state.getTask('task-1')?.assignedWorkerId).toBe('worker-1');
```
Retain the existing MODIFY_RAIL fallback test and invalid-task/rail/length coverage unchanged. Preserve existing error handling and cover persistence failure with vi.spyOn(h.state, 'writeEntity').mockRejectedValueOnce(new Error('disk full')); a valid caller-bearing invocation must reject with 'disk full' and leave proposals.size zero, rather than report success. Implement only these changes in proposeRail.ts:
```ts
// inputSchema.properties (not required):
workerId: { type: 'string', description: 'Caller worker ID (auto-injected by proxy)' }
// handler params type:
workerId?: string;
// proposal construction:
workerId: params.workerId || task.assignedWorkerId || 'unknown',
```
Do not trim supplied IDs, add role checks, change the return shape, replace existing validation, or catch/swallow createProposal errors. No hand-edits to repository .moe state; harness fixtures are isolated temporary data.
